WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.810
I met Gunter on a cold, wet and unforgettable evening in September.
我是在九月一个寒冷、潮湿、令人难忘的夜晚遇见冈特的。

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:10.410
I had planned to fly to Vienna and take a bus to Prague for a conference.
我原本打算先飞到维也纳，再坐大巴去布拉格参加一个会议。

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.000
Due to a big storm, my flight had been delayed by an hour and a half.
由于一场大暴风雨，我的航班延误了一个半小时。

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.570
I touched down in Vienna just 30 minutes before the departure of the last bus to Prague.
我在维也纳降落时，离开往布拉格的末班车发车只剩30分钟了。

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:29.510
The moment I got off the plane, I ran like crazy through the airport building and jumped into the first taxi on the rank without a second thought.
一下飞机，我就发疯似的冲过机场大楼，想都没想就跳上了候车点排在最前面的那辆出租车。

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.790
That was when I met Gunter.
就在那时，我遇见了冈特。

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.570
I told him where I was going, but he said he hadn’t heard of the bus station.
我告诉他我要去哪儿，可他说他从没听说过那个汽车站。

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:43.460
I thought my pronunciation was the problem, so I explained again more slowly, but he still looked confused.
我以为是我的发音有问题，就放慢语速又解释了一遍，可他看上去还是一脸茫然。

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.640
When I was about to give up, Gunter fished out his little phone and rang up a friend.
就在我快要放弃的时候，冈特掏出他的小手机，给一个朋友打了电话。

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.960
After a heated discussion that lasted for what seemed like a century, Gunter put his phone down and started the car.
两人激烈地讨论了一番，仿佛过了一个世纪那么久，冈特这才放下手机，发动了汽车。

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.300
Finally, with just two minutes to spare we rolled into the bus station.
终于，在只剩两分钟的时候，我们的车驶进了汽车站。

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.460
Thankfully, there was a long queue still waiting to board the bus.
谢天谢地，还有一长队人在等着上车。

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:10.950
Gunter parked the taxi behind the bus, turned around, and looked at me with a big smile on his face.
冈特把出租车停在大巴后面，转过身来，满脸笑容地看着我。

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:12.850
“We made it,” he said.
“我们赶上了。”他说。

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.750
Just then I realised that I had zero cash in my wallet.
就在这时，我意识到自己钱包里一分现金也没有。

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.010
I flashed him an apologetic smile as I pulled out my Portuguese bankcard.
我一边掏出我的葡萄牙银行卡，一边歉意地冲他一笑。

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:26.800
He tried it several times, but the card machine just did not play along.
他试了好几次，可刷卡机就是不配合。

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.740
A feeling of helplessness washed over me as I saw the bus queue thinning out.
眼看着排队等车的人越来越少，一种无助感涌上我的心头。

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.670
At this moment, Gunter pointed towards the waiting hall of the bus station.
就在这时，冈特指了指汽车站的候车大厅。

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.190
There, at the entrance, was a cash machine.
那里，入口处，有一台取款机。

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:47.940
I jumped out of the car, made a mad run for the machine, and popped my card in, only to read the message: “Out of order.
我跳下车，发疯似的冲向取款机，把卡塞了进去，结果却看到一条提示：“机器故障。

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.370
Sorry.”
抱歉。”

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.970
I ran back to Gunter and told him the bad news.
我跑回冈特身边，把这个坏消息告诉了他。

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:58.300
Four days later, when I was back in Vienna, I called Gunter as promised.
四天后，我回到维也纳，按照约定给冈特打了电话。
